{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:97533","published":"2026-11-13T06:05:11.003704Z","modified":"2026-11-13T06:30:04.483107577Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-46597"],"summary":"Important: podman security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The podman tool manages pods, container images, and containers. It is part of the libpod library, which is for applications that use container pods. Container pods is a concept in Kubernetes.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: Denial of Service via crafted AES-GCM packet decoder inputs (CVE-2026-46597)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* When using `--mount` in `podman run` results can be inconsistent, especially on /var/tmp (JIRA:Rocky Linux-154348)\n\n*  [RFE] SELinux confined users unable to start podman.socket systemd user service (JIRA:Rocky Linux-132875)\n\n* [RFE] Mounting of NFS Quadlet volume fails with permission denied (JIRA:Rocky Linux-145863)\n\n* [RFE] podman API socket to support TLS/mTLS (JIRA:Rocky Linux-91221)\n\n* Rebase podman to the latest upstream release [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-168737)\n\n* podman does not clean up all files and leaves orphaned files consuming disk space [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-173976)\n\n* [FJ9.8 Bug]: [REG]The \"podman-remote save\" command fails for rootless users. (JIRA:Rocky Linux-186006)\n\n* podman: rebase to 5.8.5 (JIRA:Rocky Linux-212537)\n\n* [FJ9.9 Bug]: [REG]The \"podman rm\" command can accidentally delete containers even though it is mounted by Buildah when used by a rootless user in remote. (JIRA:Rocky Linux-211092)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Rocky Linux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"podman","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6:5.8.5-2.el9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97533.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6:5.8.5-2.el9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97533.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-debugsource","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman-debugsource?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6:5.8.5-2.el9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97533.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-plugins","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman-plugins?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6:5.8.5-2.el9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97533.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-plugins-debuginfo","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman-plugins-debuginfo?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6:5.8.5-2.el9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97533.json"}},{"package":{"name":"podman-remote","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/podman-remote?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=6"},"ranges":[{"t